{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Fifty.</b> Now he mentions the number of loops." "<b>And the word מקבילות.</b> This one opposite that one. Some say it is like ויכהו קבל עם (2 Kings 15:10) and מחי קבלו (Ezekiel 26:11), and the meaning [is] opposite." "<b>אשה</b> [is] an independent noun, and likewise איש; therefore והאיש גבריאל (Daniel 9:21)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "The Hebrew comment breaks off mid-sentence after ופירוש; the Ezekiel reference given as יחז׳ is an abbreviation for Ezekiel, here resolved."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:31.017268249Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}